  "short_description": "Dahua 2 MP HDCVI quick-install eyeball, 3.6 mm lens, 30 m smart IR, 4-in-1 CVI/TVI/AHD/CVBS output, 12 V DC, IP50 dust-protected. Indoor or sheltered use.",
  "long_description": "## What it is\n\nThe Dahua HAC-HDW1200TRQ (ordering code DH-HAC-HDW1200TRQP for PAL) is the S6 version of Dahua's 2 MP Lite Series HDCVI eyeball camera. It is a white plastic turret, 97.1 mm across and 93 mm tall, weighing 0.14 kg, with a 3.6 mm fixed M12 lens that gives an 83° horizontal field of view. The body sits on a quick-to-install pedestal that screws straight to the surface. This base TRQP model has no microphone. It is rated IP50 — protected against dust but not against water — so it belongs indoors or under cover.\n\n## What it's for\n\nIt is the workhorse camera for homes, shops, small offices, apartment corridors and godowns running on Dahua HDCVI or any 4-in-1 DVR. The single BNC output switches between CVI, TVI, AHD and CVBS, so it can replace an old analogue camera on the existing coaxial cable without changing the recorder.\n\n## Key specifications\n\nThe 2 MP progressive-scan CMOS sensor produces 1920 × 1080 video at up to 30 fps, with 960H output available on CVBS. Minimum illumination is 0.01 lux, and two smart-IR LEDs light the scene in black and white to about 30 m — further than most 2 MP cameras in this class. The bracket pans 360°, tilts 78° and rotates 360°. Power is 12 V DC at a maximum of 2.7 W. It is rated for −40 °C to 60 °C at up to 95% humidity. The datasheet lists IEC/EN 62368-1 safety and EN 55032/55035 and FCC Part 15B EMC compliance. Warranty is 24 months.\n\n## Installation notes\n\nFix the pedestal to a ceiling or wall at around 2.7 m, clip the eyeball on, and aim using the three adjustment axes. Keep it away from rain, splash and wash-down areas — IP50 is a dust rating only, and the camera is not rated for outdoor use. Run coaxial cable to the DVR and set the DVR channel to the CVI mode (or TVI/AHD for other recorders). Use a regulated 12 V DC supply sized for 2.7 W per camera. If sound recording is needed, specify the HAC-HDW1200TRQ-A variant instead.\n\n## What's in the box\n\nOne camera with quick-install pedestal, video and power pigtail, mounting screws and wall plugs, a drilling template and a quick start guide, in a single printed carton.",
